    labsNotIncludedNotice.jspf: names the attached lab results that the consultation PDF could not
    include, on the pages that confirm a print or a fax (issue #4693).

    Why: the consultation PDF can draw HL7 lab reports only. A CML, MDS or PathNet (BCP) lab, or an
    attachment whose source was never recorded, is left out of the packet and named instead on a
    page right after the consultation letter. This block tells the sender the same thing, so a
    missing lab is not first noticed by the clinician who receives the fax.

    Reads the request attribute consultLabsNotIncluded (ConsultationLabsNotIncluded.REQUEST_ATTRIBUTE),
    a List<String> of names already in the reader's language, set by
    DocumentAttachmentManager.renderConsultationFormWithAttachments. Renders nothing when the
    attribute is absent or empty. The names carry lab disciplines and dates, so each one is
    HTML-encoded; the block only appears in the response to the user who printed or faxed them.

    Usage, once per page, inside <body>:
        <%@ include file="/WEB-INF/jsp/encounter/oscarConsultationRequest/labsNotIncludedNotice.jspf" %>

    @since 2026-10-16
--%>
<%@ taglib uri="jakarta.tags.core" prefix="c" %>
<%@ taglib uri="jakarta.tags.fmt" prefix="fmt" %>
<%@ taglib uri="carlos" prefix="carlos" %>
<fmt:setBundle basename="oscarResources"/>
<c:if test="${not empty consultLabsNotIncluded}">
    <div id="consultLabsNotIncluded" class="alert alert-warning text-start py-2 px-3 mb-3" role="alert" style="font-size:0.85rem;">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation me-1"></i>
        <fmt:message key="encounter.oscarConsultationRequest.ConfirmConsultationRequest.msgLabsNotIncluded"/>
        <ul class="mb-0 mt-1">
            <c:forEach items="${consultLabsNotIncluded}" var="labNotIncluded">
                <li><carlos:encode value="${labNotIncluded}"/></li>
            </c:forEach>
        </ul>
    </div>
</c:if>
